George,

My guess is that because you only have one treated unit, it's not
calculating the mean correctly for the treatment group.  It definitely
would not calculate any of the empirical quantile statistics on one
observation.  If you really wanted the mean different, it would simply be
your treated Y minus the mean of the control Ys before matching, and your
treated Y minus your control Y after matching.  You can do those pretty
easily manually.

