Hi Machteld,
Unfortunately I do not know of any way to implement a standard "Rosenbaum" style sensitivity analysis following full matching, at least not in rbounds.

But there are some other sensitivity analysis procedures out there, including this one:
http://www.tommasonannicini.eu/Portals/0/sensatt_wp_4.pdf

You could see if that one could be implemented following full matching; I am not sure.

I will also send you (off the listserv so as not to spam everyone) a manuscript I have in press that discusses some of these approaches, some of which you would be able to use with full matching.  They rely on slightly different procedures and assumptions than the Rosenbaum approach, but with the same sort of general idea.

Liz


